  'tshwane-water-interruptions-region-4-reservoirs-critical-2026-11-22',
  'Tshwane warns of low water pressure as Region 4 reservoirs run critically low',
  'Utilities', '2026-11-22', 'Rekord', 'https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/2026/11/22/tshwane-to-implement-further-water-supply-measures-amid-low-pressure-in-region-4/',
  'The City of Tshwane says a weaker, lower-pressure feed from Rand Water''s Palmiet system has left reservoirs in Region 4 and parts of Regions 1 and 3 critically low, and it is warning of more interruptions.',
  'The City of Tshwane said on Sunday that its Region 4 reservoirs, along with parts of Regions 1 and 3, are under strain because Rand Water''s Palmiet system is delivering less water at a lower pressure than the network needs. The metro said some customers living in these areas could see weaker taps or supply cuts until the affected reservoirs have had a chance to refill.

In Region 1, the city named the Soshanguve L reservoirs and tower, along with the Mabopane Main Reservoir, as critically low, while the Ga-Rankuwa Industrial, Klipgat and Kruisfontein systems are under pressure. In Region 3, the Atteridgeville LL system is under pressure and the Klapperkop Reservoir is low, though the Heights reservoirs still hold some water.

Region 4 is among the hardest hit: the city listed the Laudium Reservoir and the Atteridgeville HL Reservoir as critically low, and said both compartments of the Rooihuiskraal reservoirs are effectively empty. The Heuweloord Reservoir is also low, and supply to Brakfontein, Bakenkop, Louwlardia, Doringkloof and Clifton remains constrained.

By contrast, the city said Region 2, covering Wonderboom, Magalieskruin, Sinoville and Montana, is receiving a relatively stable supply, helped by the Roodeplaat Water Treatment Plant. The metro said its teams are intervening operationally to even out what supply is available so reservoirs get a chance to fill back up, and are keeping a close eye on storage levels whenever demand spikes.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/2026/11/22/tshwane-to-implement-further-water-supply-measures-amid-low-pressure-in-region-4/", "https://iol.co.za/news/south-africa/2026-11-22-tshwane-warns-of-water-interruptions-as-reservoirs-reach-critical-levels/"]',
  'agent'
);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news (
  slug, title, category, published_date, source_name, source_url,
  summary, body, image_url, image_credit, image_source, verification_json, source
) VALUES (
  'loftus-road-closures-sundowns-chiefs-carling-knockout-2026-11-22',
  'Streets around Loftus closed Sunday for Sundowns-Chiefs cup semi-final',
  'Traffic', '2026-11-22', 'Rekord', 'https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/2026/11/22/loftus-stadium-road-closures-streets-to-avoid-during-sundowns-and-chiefs-match/',
  'Tshwane Metro Police shut streets around Loftus Versfeld from 08:00 to 20:00 on Sunday for the Carling Knockout semi-final between Mamelodi Sundowns and Kaizer Chiefs.',
  'The Tshwane Metro Police Department (TMPD) closed a number of streets around Loftus Versfeld Stadium from 08:00 to 20:00 on Sunday for the Carling Knockout Cup semi-final between Mamelodi Sundowns and Kaizer Chiefs, which kicked off at 15:30.

TMPD spokesperson Lieutenant Colonel Isaac Mahamba said the affected intersections included Park Street at Farenden Street, Ayton Street, Beckett Street, Orient Street and Kirkness Street, as well as Farenden Street at Arcadia Street, Eastwood Street at Arcadia Street, Lynnwood Street at Walton Jameson Avenue, Lynnwood Road at University Road, Walton Jameson Street at Villa Street and Bond Street, Brecher Street at Walton Jameson Avenue, and Maple Street at Ivy Street and Myrtle Street.

Motorists needing to get around the stadium were pointed toward a set of detours: Francis Baard Street and Pretorius Street on one side, Stanza Bopape Street and Justice Mahomed Street further out, with Leyds Street, Middel Street, Jan Shoba Street and Florence Ribeiro Avenue offered as further options. TMPD officers worked alongside the South African Police Service to keep watch over traffic on the affected streets for the duration of the closures.

The winner of the semi-final advances to the Carling Knockout final on 12 December against Orlando Pirates, who booked their place by beating Stellenbosch FC 2-0 in their own semi-final at Moses Mabhida Stadium.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/2026/11/22/loftus-stadium-road-closures-streets-to-avoid-during-sundowns-and-chiefs-match/", "https://www.archyde.com/sundowns-host-chiefs-in-carling-knockout-semi-final-sunday-at-loftus/"]',
  'agent'
);
